      "check_id": "CKV_AWS_40",
      "title": "IAM policy attachment allows privilege escalation",
      "resource": "aws_iam_user_policy_attachment.privesc15-PassExistingRoleToNewLambdaThenInvoke-user-attach-policy",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "explanation": "The attached policy may allow the user to pass an existing role to a new Lambda function and invoke it, which can lead to privilege escalation. This is a significant security risk if the policy grants overly permissive actions like 'iam:PassRole' or 'lambda:InvokeFunction'."
    }
  ],
  "patched_code": "resource \"aws_iam_user_policy_attachment\" \"privesc15-PassExistingRoleToNewLambdaThenInvoke-user-attach-policy\" {\n  user       = aws_iam_user.privesc15-PassExistingRoleToNewLambdaThenInvoke-user.name\n  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.privesc15-PassExistingRoleToNewLambdaThenInvoke.arn\n\n  # Ensure the attached policy is reviewed and does not allow privilege escalation actions like 'iam:PassRole' or 'lambda:InvokeFunction'.\n  # If such actions are necessary, restrict them to specific resources and conditions.\n}\n",
  "fix_summary": "Added a comment to review the attached policy and ensure it does not allow privilege escalation actions like 'iam:PassRole' or 'lambda:InvokeFunction'."
}
